Fares are set by the [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor]] board and are integrated with the metro's [[Tarifa Integrada]] system, which allows free transfers between the ferry and metro services within a 90-minute window. The Route 1 Pandao crossing and Route 6 Platja de Jordi crossing are both included in the standard metro zone 1 fare, making them the cheapest crossings on the network and reinforcing their role as the primary commuter links across the bay.

Concession fares (half price) are available to seniors, students, and children under 12. Children under 5 travel free. Monthly passes are available for Routes 1, 3, 4, 6, and 7, which serve regular commuters; Routes 2 and 5, which are primarily recreational, do not offer monthly passes.

Illa Daurada residents are eligible for a discounted '''Illenc pass''' — a monthly pass for Route 3 at a reduced rate of $95, subsidised by the [[Municipalitat de les Illes]] — reflecting the island community's dependence on the ferry for daily access to the mainland.

Route 5 (Parc Nacional wetlands) fares include the park entrance fee, which is collected on behalf of the [[Parc Nacional de la Marjal]] authority.

